# Personal IDE AI Configuration
#
# These are per-IDE COPIES of the BMAD skills, written by the installer from the
# tracked `_bmad/` framework install. They are 100% regenerable — recreate them
# with `npx bmad-method@<version> install` (the pinned version lives in
# _bmad/_config/manifest.yaml). Tracking them buys nothing and made every BMAD
# update a ~200-file diff.
#
# NOTE: .agents/ and .github/agents/ are the CURRENT installer output paths.
# .gemini/ and .github/copilot/ are the pre-6.x paths, kept so an older install
# or a stale working copy can't leak back in.
.claude/
.agents/
.github/agents/
.gemini/
.github/copilot/

# _bmad-output/ is TRACKED. It holds the live PRD, architecture, epics and every
# story record — the only copy that describes what was actually built. The old
# comment here read "artifacts are project-specific, not framework", which is
# exactly backwards as a reason to ignore them: project-specific is what belongs
# in the project's repo. The framework itself (_bmad/) is the regenerable half.

# A ~9MB BMAD documentation dump, re-downloadable by the installer.
docs/llms-full.txt

# BMAD personal install answers (user_name, communication_language, skill level).
# The team-wide equivalents live in the tracked _bmad/config.toml and
# _bmad/custom/config.toml; this file is per-developer and the installer
# recreates it. Its sibling _bmad/custom/config.user.toml is already ignored by
# _bmad/custom/.gitignore.
_bmad/config.user.toml

